// `@heap` states something only an `extern fn` can need said: that C the compiler cannot read touches the heap.
// A kama body's allocations are already seen, so on a body the attribute would be a second, unchecked claim
// about the same thing — refused by name rather than as an unknown attribute (KR-47).
@heap fn int32 f() { return 0; }
fn int32 main() { return f(); }
